  "security_implications": "If ClearStatusOnFatalAlert is 0, the recoverable error status bit in hw2reg.status.alert_recov_ctrl_update_err is not cleared when a fatal alert is asserted, potentially leaking recoverable error information after a fatal security event. Additionally, the fatal alert storage input ctrl_err_storage_d relies on the assumption that ctrl_reg_err_storage and shadowed_storage_err_i remain asserted until reset; if they do not, a fatal alert could be lost, violating the security requirement that fatal alerts persist until reset.",
